+
+# Scope and observed boundary
+
+This local audit retains CoreX compiled TTGIR, LLVM IR, binaries, metadata, and three independent process runs for tile-order and dual-accumulator GEMM variants. The 256³ FP16 GEMM `num_stages=2/3` TTGIR contains `triton_gpu.insert_slice_async`, `async_commit_group`, and `async_wait`; shared memory increases from 4 KiB at one stage to 8/12 KiB. The earlier stage-7 timing found no speedup for more stages in this small case. These are compiler-intermediate observations, not a claim of NVIDIA TMA or mbarrier-equivalent hardware instructions.
+
+`tl.swizzle2d` rearranged program tile IDs. This is separate from shared-memory bank swizzling. It passed correctness on three GEMM shapes, but three-round speedup was near one. A dual-accumulator K loop passed all shapes but was about 0.937× versus the single accumulator at 512³; it does not implement SM100 TMEM ping-pong.
+
+`enable_warp_specialization=True` was accepted by the JIT for one GEMM, but its TTGIR and LLVM IR hashes exactly matched the default variant and resource metadata matched. This does not establish target warp specialization. A direct `enable_persistent=True` launch keyword was rejected by this JIT function. The retained vendor compiler excerpt and SHA identify the architecture guard in the installed build.
+
+The exact protocol, performance ratios, and limits are reported in the repository `experiments/kernelwiki_iluvatar/PROJECT_REPORT_AND_NEXT_PLAN.md`. Raw source and receipts are self-contained under `evidence/bi-v150-corex42-scheduling-audit/`.
+
+## Larger GEMM stage-count replication
+
+The same FP16 GEMM+bias tile was checked against CPU FP64 reference on 512x512x2048 and 1024x1024x1024, with three independent process runs and paired alternating GPU-event timing. Stage 2 vs stage 1 gave 1.0154x and 1.0018x geometric-mean speedup; stage 3 gave 0.7724x and 0.9166x. All outputs passed atol=rtol=0.03. Thus extra stages are not a general optimization rule on this target and tile. Raw samples, source, and SHA256 receipts are under `stage10-pipeline-scaling/`; the full interpretation is in repository `experiments/kernelwiki_iluvatar/PROJECT_REPORT_AND_NEXT_PLAN.md`.
+
+## Dtype and tile holdout
+
+Three independent processes checked FP16/BF16, 32x32x32/64x64x32 tiles, two larger GEMM+bias shapes, and stages 1/2/3 against a CPU FP64 reference. All 72 candidate checks passed. Stage 2 gave 1.0162x for BF16 long-K with the 32 tile but 0.9152x for BF16 1024-cubed with the 64 tile; stage 3 was 0.7484x for the latter. The full eight-case matrix and scope are in repository `experiments/kernelwiki_iluvatar/PROJECT_REPORT_AND_NEXT_PLAN.md`. Raw rounds, script, and SHA256 receipts are under `stage11-pipeline-holdout/`. These results guide target-side parameter search and do not establish NVIDIA hardware equivalence.
